{"document_id": "a549d4d1cc6d6f361c442659296c9a3f59f8a6da20cd2472d96a87db91f8fd2b", "canonical_type": "Notification", "document_type": "Notification", "document_title": "Deferred Payment of Import Duty (Amendment) Rules, 2026", "document_jurisdiction": "Central", "issuing_authority": "Government of India, Ministry of Finance (Department of Revenue), Central Board of Indirect Taxes and Customs", "issue_date": "2026-02-01", "text": "[TO BE PUBLISHED IN THE GAZETTE OF INDIA, EXTRAORDINARY, PART II, SECTION 3, SUB-SECTION(i)]\nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA MINISTRY OF FINANCE (DEPARTMENT OF REVENUE) (CENTRAL BOARD OF INDIRECT TAXES AND CUSTOMS)\nNotification\n[No. 13/2026-Customs (N.T.)]\nNew Delhi, the 1[st] February, 2026\nG.S.R....(E). - In exercise of the powers conferred by the proviso to sub-section (1) of section 47 and section 156 of the Customs Act, 1962 (52 of 1962), the Central Government hereby makes the following rules further to amend the Deferred Payment of Import Duty Rules, 2016, namely: —\n1. Short title and commencement: - (1) These rules may be called the Deferred Payment of Import Duty (Amendment) Rules, 2026.\n(2) They shall come into force on the 1[st ] day of March, 2026.\n2.\nIn the Deferred Payment of Import Duty Rules, 2016, in rule 4, for clauses (a) to (c), the following clauses shall be substituted, namely:—\n“(a) for goods corresponding to Bill of Entry returned for payment from 1[st] day to the last day of any month other than March, the duty shall be paid by the 1[st] day of the following month;\n(b) for goods corresponding to Bill of Entry returned for payment from 1[st] day to 31[st] day of March, the duty shall be paid by 31[st] March.”.\n[F. No 450/04/2026- Cus IV]\n(Anurima Sharma) Director (Customs)\nNote: The principal rules were published in the Gazette of India, Extraordinary, Part II, Section 3, Sub-section (i), dated the 2[nd] November, 2016 vide number G.S.R. 1037 (E ), dated the 2[nd] November, 2016 and was last amended vide number G.S.R. 585 (E), dated the 3[rd] August, 2023.", "source": "KanoonGPT/indian-legal-documents"}
{"document_id": "1d8977076663497fda72d94d17df6d35539728283f0bd39830539d53288c1a1d", "canonical_type": "Notification", "document_type": "Notification", "document_title": "Gujarat Textile Policy -2024 (Amendment)", "document_jurisdiction": "State (Gujarat)", "issuing_authority": "Government of Gujarat, Industries and Mines Department", "issue_date": "2026-01-31", "text": "Letter No: IMD/0570/01/2026 Approved Date: 31-01-2026\nGujarat Textile Policy -2024 (Amendment)\nGovernment of Gujarat Industries and Mines Department Sachivalaya, Gandhinagar Resolution No. IMD/WRT/e-file/9/2023/2817/CH Dated. As per E-sign\nRead:-\n1. Industries and Mines Department GR No. IMD/WRT/e-file/9/2023/2817/CH, dated 15/10/2024\nAmendment:-\nIn Para No. 3.17, 3.19, and 5.5.2(a) in GR dated: 15/10/2024 read at (1) above, the present provisions are amended hereby as under.\nPara\nPresent Provision\nAmended Provision\n3.17\nCategory-wise classifcation of talukas will be as per the Industries and Mines Department GR MIS-102020- 347965-I dated 2/11/2020. If a project is located within the geographical limit of more than one taluka, then the taluka in which the project has the largest percentage of land area will be considered as the eligible category of taluka under the Policy. An Industrial Undertaking located within the limit of Municipal Corporation (notifed as on date) will not be eligible for incentives under the Policy.\nCategory-wise classifcation of talukas will be as per the Industries and Mines Department GR MIS-102020- 347965-I dated 2/11/2020. If a project is located within the geographical limit of more than one taluka, then the taluka in which the project has the largest percentage of land area will be considered as the eligible category of taluka under the Policy. Only those industrial undertakings located within the limits of a Municipal Corporation (as notifed on date) and engaged in eligible non-polluting activities such as garment, apparel and made-ups, stitching, embroidery, and other activities falling under the Green/White category or its equivalent categories, as defned and amended from time to time by the GPCB, will be considered eligible for incentives under thepolicy.\n3.19\nSelf Help Group meansGroup of SHGs duly registered with NRLM/NULM or any voluntarily group of at least 25 women with mutual agreement to contribute to a common cause of the group and is self-governed and forms an association of people hailing from similar socio- economic background with the objective to collectively fulfll the common purpose to improve the livelihood conditions.\nSelf Help Group meansSHG or Group of SHGs duly registered with NRLM/NULM or any voluntarily group of at least 25 women with mutual agreement to contribute to a common cause of the group and is self-governed and forms an association of people hailing from similar socio- economic background with the objective to collectively fulfll the common purpose to improve the livelihood conditions.\n5.5.2(a)\nSHG having 25 or more women will be eligible for assistance.\nSHG As per defnition mentioned in para 3.19 will be eligible for assistance.\nOther Provisions of the GR Dated 15/10/2024 read at (1) will remain unchanged.\nThis issues with the approval of the Government dated 22/01/2026 on this Department’s File of even number.\nBy order and in the name of the Governor of Gujarat,\n(J. B. Patel) Joint Secretary (Industries) Industries and Mines Department\nCopy To:-\n1. Secretary to Hon. Governor of Gujarat, Rajbhavan, Gandhinagar (By Letter)\n2. Principal Secretary to Hon. Chief Minister, sachivalaya, Gandhinagar.\n3. Personal Secretary to Hon. Deputy Chief Minister, sachivalaya, Gandhinagar.\n4. Personal Secretary to all Hon. Ministers/Minister of State, Sachivalaya, Gandhinagar\nFile No: IMD/WRT/e-file/9/2023/2817/CH Section - Small Industries\nApproved By: Joint Secretary,CH Section - Small Industries,IMD\n==> picture [320 x 15] intentionally omitted <==\n==> picture [95 x 55] intentionally omitted <==\n1/2\nLetter No: IMD/0570/01/2026 Approved Date: 31-01-2026\n5. Joint Secretary to Chief Secretary, Sachivalaya, Gandhinagar\n6. Additional Chief Secretary, Finance Department, Sachivalaya, Gandhinagar\n7. Additional Chief Secretary, Industries and Mines Department, Sachivalaya, Gandhinagar\n8. Additional Chief Secretary, Revenue Department, Sachivalaya, Gandhinagar\n9. Additional Chief Secretary, Energy & Petrochemicals Department, Sachivalaya, Gandhinagar\n10. Chief Commissioner of State Tax, Gujarat State, Rajyakar bhavan, Ahmedabad\n11. Industries Commissioner, Udyog Bhavan, Gandhinagar\n-\n12.Managing Director, GIDC, Udyog Bhavan, Gandhinagar\n13. Commissioner of Cottage and Rural Industries, Udyog Bhavan, Gandhinagar.\n-\n14.Commissioner MSME, Gandhinagar.\n15. Secretary, Gujarat Electricity Regulatory Commission, Ashram Road, Ahmedabad.\n-\n16.Director of Employment and Training, Dr. Jivraj Mehta Bhavan, Gandhinagar.\n17. Commissioner of Information, Dr. Jivraj Mehta Bhavan, Gandhinagar.\n-\n18.All District Industries Centers (Through Industries Commissioner)\n19. All Departments of Sachivalaya, Gandhinagar.\n20. The President, Gujarat Chamber of Commerce and Industries, Ashram Road, Ahmedabad\n21. I.T. Branch, Industries and Mines Department, Sachivalaya, Gandhinagar\n-\n22.Accountant General Rajkot/Ahmedabad\n-\n23.Select File\nPage 1 of 2\nSignature Not Verified\nSigned by:J B Patel Joint Secretary Date:2026.01.31 17:56:52 +5:30\nFile No: IMD/WRT/e-file/9/2023/2817/CH Section - Small Industries Approved By: Joint Secretary,CH Section - Small Industries,IMD\n==> picture [320 x 15] intentionally omitted <==\n==> picture [95 x 55] intentionally omitted <==\n2/2", "source": "KanoonGPT/indian-legal-documents"}
{"document_id": "628544458d6a90dd87486eab6029916df8ee62b132b07b3713f02e8a18e48130", "canonical_type": "Notification", "document_type": "Notification", "document_title": "Telangana Civil Services (Classification, Control and Appeal) Rules, 1991 - Rule 9 and 25 - Amendments — Notification", "document_jurisdiction": "State (Telangana)", "issuing_authority": "General Administration (Services-C) Department, Government of Telangana", "issue_date": "2026-01-23", "text": "—\ni\n. t } J\n—\n[ru\n:\nGOVERNMENT OF TELANGANA ABSTRACT\nPublic Services — Telangana Civil Services (Classification, Control and Appeal) Rules, 1991 - Rule 9 and 25 - Amendments — Notification - Orders — Issued.\nd\nG.0.MS.No.!\nGENERAL ADMINISTRATION (SERVICES-C) DEPARTMENT\nDated:23.01.2026\nORDER:\n1%\nThe following notification will be published in the Telangana Gazette:\nb 0 +o\nNOTIFICATION\nIn exercise of the powers conferred by the proviso to article 309 of the Constitution of India and of all other powers hereunto enabling, the Governor of Telangana hereby makes the following amendments to the Telangana Civil Services (Classification, Control and Appeal) Rules, 1991, issued in G.0.Ms.N0.487, General Administration (Services-C) Department, Dated the 14\" September, 1992 and published in Part-I, No.235, extraordinary issue of the Andhra Pradesh Gazette, dated the 1% July, 1992, as adapted by the Government of Telangana vide G.0.Ms.No.190, General Administration (Ser.C) Department, dated the 27\" May, 2016, as subsequently amended from time to time.\nl=\n20\nADDENDA\n1.\nIn the said rules, in rule 9,-\n-\n(1) in clause (ix), for the expression “;\", the expression *:” shall be substituted;\n-\n(2) after clause (ix) so amended, the following provisos shall be inserted, namely,\n-\n“Provided that a Government Servant shall be deemed to have been removed from service, if he/she,\n-\nPda absent from duty without authorization for a period exceeding one year; or\n-\n(b) remains absent from duty for a continuous period exceeding five (5) years with or without leave; or\n-\n(c) continues on foreign service beyond the period approved by the State Government:\nProvided further that a show cause notice to explain the reasons for such absence from duty or continuation on foreign service shall be given to the Government Servant and his/her reply shall be considered before invoking the above said proviso.”.\n2.\nIn rule 25, in clause (i), after the word “or”, the following shall be inserted, namely,“Misconduct leads to a penalty imposed as per first proviso to clause (ix) of rule 9 of\nthese rules, or”\n(BY ORDER AND IN THE NAME OF THE GOVERNOR OF TELANGANA)\nK.RAMAKRISHNA RAO CHIEF SECRETARY TO GOVERNMENT\n2! The Commissioner of Printing, Stationary & Stores Purchase, Hyderabad. (with a request to publish in the Telangana Gazette Extraordinary and supply 200 copies). 20 fo L4 All Departments of Secretariat. Tree, ds of Departments. Ail District Collectors.\nCopy to: The Registrar, High Court for the State of Telangana, Hyderabad. All Service Sections in General Administration Department. The Secretary to Vigilance Commissioner, Telangana Vigilance Commission, Hyderabad. The Secretary, Telangana Public Service Commission, Hyderabad. The Law (A) Department i The Finance (HRM.III) Department, Telangana Secretariat, Hyderabad. h SF/SC. 5 «<SSvar Gg,7 of / EH) /] FORWARDED:: BY ORDER // SECTION OFFICER\nt\n1\n==> picture [333 x 71] intentionally omitted <==\n----- Start of picture text -----\nHIGH COURT FOR THE STATE OF TELANGANA:: HYDERABAD FAKE E. 2026 Dt. || ----- End of picture text -----\n-\nDt. ||.02.2026\n“COMMUNICATED\"\n==> picture [147 x 30] intentionally omitted <==\n----- Start of picture text -----\nWiad REGISTRAR GENERAL ----- End of picture text -----\n==> picture [12 x 8] intentionally omitted <==\n----- Start of picture text -----\nTo ----- End of picture text -----\n1.\nThe Prl. Secretary to the Hon'ble the Chief Justice, High Court for the State of Telangana, Hyderabad.\n2.\nAll the P.Ss to the Hon'ble Judges, High Court for the State of Telangana, Hyderabad.\n3.\nAll the Registrars, High Court for the State of Telangana, Hyderabad.\n4.\nAll the Unit Heads in the State of Telangana.\n5.\nThe Section Officers, Establishment Section,[C] Section, B.Spl. Section[&][B] Section, High Court for the State of Telangana.\n6.\nThe Section Officer, Enquiry Cell Section, High Court for the State of Telangana\n-\n(with a request to communicate to the Presenting Officer).\nOFFICE OF THE PRINCIPAL[DISTRICT][AND][SESSIONS][JUDGE:] YADADRI-BHUVANAGIRI. Lr.Dis.No. 377 /2026/A1, Dated: 2 3-01-2026.\n“Communicated”.\nTo\npy ru piste NS E, YADADRI-BHUVANAG |\nAll the Judicial Officers in the Yadadri-Bhongir District Unit.", "source": "KanoonGPT/indian-legal-documents"}
